<li <%= tag.attributes(**step_options) %>>
  <div class="workflow-step-marker">
    <% if connector_state %>
      <span class="<%= connector_classes %>" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <% end %>
    <% if dot? %>
      <span class="<%= dot_classes %>" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <% else %>
      <span class="<%= circle_classes %>">
        <% if circle_number? %>
          <%= number %>
        <% else %>
          <%= render Bali::Icon::Component.new(circle_icon, size: 16) %>
        <% end %>
      </span>
    <% end %>
    <%# Both markers say the state in colour and nothing else — the number is a
        position, not a verdict, and the dot has no text at all. This is the one
        place that says it in words, and it sits outside the circle so the
        number stays the circle's whole content. %>
    <span class="sr-only"><%= state_label %></span>
  </div>
  <div class="workflow-step-body">
    <p class="<%= title_classes %>"><%= title %></p>
    <% if assignee.present? %>
      <p class="workflow-step-assignee">
        <%= render Bali::Icon::Component.new("user", size: 14) %>
        <%= assignee %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <% if date.present? %>
      <p class="workflow-step-date"><%= date %></p>
    <% end %>
    <%# `content?` only says that a block was passed, not that it rendered
        anything. A host writes "the comment, if there is one" by putting the
        conditional inside the block, so every step passes one and `content?`
        is true on all of them — leaving an empty `.workflow-step-comment`
        behind, dragging its `mt-1`. `content.present?` asks the rendered
        string instead, and `blank?` already covers the whitespace-only block.
        Reading it here costs no second render: ViewComponent memoises the
        capture, so the `content` below is that same string.

        Keep this comment free of ERB tags: a comment opened with an ERB tag
        ends at the first closing delimiter, wherever it sits, so an example
        quoted in the prose truncates it and spills the rest into the step
        body as plain text. Describe the host's conditional in words. %>
    <% if content.present? %>
      <div class="workflow-step-comment"><%= content %></div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</li>
